{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Going up and descending on it — going up</b> first and afterwards <b>descending</b>, and remaining below — like a person who goes up from the house to the upper story and afterwards descends in the house and remains in the house. And because of this he said, 'this is none other than the house of Elohim' — that is to say, their dwelling is here, and therefore they go up first; and were their dwelling not here but only temporary, it should have said 'descending and going up.' In the Jerusalem Targum it explains: the angels who were appointed to escort him were going up on high to announce to the other angels, 'Come below and see Jacob, the beloved in appearance, whose likeness is engraved on the Throne of Glory.' And the angels were going up and descending and gazing at him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:27.789276714Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}